  "step_2": "The individual chooses Lottery A. In the verbal report, the individual states: 'Ich entscheide mich für A, da ich nur die hälfte verlieren würde als bei Lotterie B. Den minimalen Unterscheid von 0,01% nehme ich in kauf.' This translates to: 'I choose A because I would only lose half as much as in Lottery B. I accept the minimal difference of 0.01%.' The individual is focusing on the amount of loss (3000 vs. 6000 Euros) and the small difference in probability (0.2% vs. 0.1%). The individual does not mention skewness or the distribution of probabilities in terms of right-skewness. Instead, the justification centers on the magnitude of the loss and the small probability difference. The individual does not refer to the probability of unfavorable outcomes or the shape of the distribution. The deliberation is based on expected loss or loss magnitude, not on skewness. The individual's reasoning is about the size of the loss (half as much) and willingness to accept a small probability difference, not about the proportion of probability mass on negative outcomes. Thus, the information considered is about loss amount and probability difference, not skewness.",
