y A has only 50%. So Lottery B is more right-skewed under this definition. Therefore, the decision reason would prefer Lottery B. However, the reason as stated is logically inconsistent with standard terminology. Still, based on the given definition, we can apply it: the reason prefers the lottery with greater probability assigned to unfavorable outcomes. So, the relevant information is: Lottery A: 50% unfavorable (loss of 1000), Lottery B: 100% unfavorable (loss of 500). Thus, Lottery B is more right-skewed under the given definition. The decision reason applies and can be used to evaluate the lotteries.",
